{title: Will the Circle Be Unbroken}
{artist: Ada R. Habershon / Charles H. Gabriel}
{genre: Gospel}
{style: Traditional}
{flow: Closing}
{key: G}
{key_original: Ab}
{tempo: 92}
{time: 4/4}
{c: Chords checked against the four-part harmony of the Cyber Hymnal score (The Greatest Hymns, by George C. Stebbins & Reuben A. Torrey (Chicago, Illinois: Tabernacle Publishing, ca. 1924), # 339)}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[G]There are loved ones in the glory,
[G]Whose dear [C]forms you often [G]miss;
[G]When you close your earthly story,
[G]Will you [D]join them [A7]in their [D]bliss?
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[G]Will the circle be unbroken
[G]By and [C]by, by and [G]by?
[G]In a [C]better home a[G]waiting
[G]In the sky, in the sky?
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[G]In the joyous days of childhood,
[G]Oft they [C]told of wondrous [G]love,
[G]Pointed to the dying Savior
[G]Now they [D]dwell with [A7]Him a[D]bove.
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[G]You remember songs of Heaven
[G]Which you [C]sang with childish [G]voice,
[G]Do you love the hymns they taught you,
[G]Or are [D]songs of [A7]earth your [D]choice?
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[G]You can picture happy gatherings
[G]Round the [C]fireside long a[G]go,
[G]And you think of tearful partings,
[G]When they [D]left you [A7]here be[D]low:
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 5}
[G]One by one their seats were emptied,
[G]One by [C]one they went a[G]way;
[G]Here the circle has been broken—
[G]Will it [D]be com[A7]plete one [D]day?
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}
